---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import manifest from '../../generated/sim/manifest.json';
import '../../styles/prose.css';

const kernels = Object.values(manifest.kernels);
---

<Layout
  title="Licenses for the RTOS lessons and simulator - OSRTOS"
  description="Licenses of the lesson text, the kernel source excerpts and the simulator used in the OSRTOS lessons."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold">Licenses</h1>

    <h2>Lesson text</h2>
    <p>
      The text of the lessons is available under the
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike License</a>,
      like most of the text on this site.
    </p>

    <h2>Kernel source code</h2>
    <p>
      The lessons show excerpts of real kernel source code, and the simulator's kernel models are ports of
      that code. Both stay under the license of the kernel they come from, at these pinned versions:
    </p>
    <ul>
      {kernels.map(kernel => (
        <li>
          <a href={kernel.repo} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{kernel.name}</a> {kernel.version}:
          <a href={kernel.licenseUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{kernel.license} license</a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <h2>Simulator</h2>
    <p>
      The simulator bundle and its generated data files carry their own licenses and are not covered by the
      Creative Commons license above. The full notices are in
      <a href="/sim/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt">THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
